# LAST AISLE - plants.art
# Mutated vegetation seen from directly above. Light from the top-left, 1px dark outline ('1') so they hold on
# grass, dirt and lino alike.
# Rooted plants (spitter, nettle) are two layers: a still _base leaf rosette (pivot 8,8 = the stalk, never rotated;
# its 2 frames are variants, not an animation) and a _head drawn on top that the engine turns towards its prey.
# Heads face RIGHT (+x); the stalk leaves the rosette at the head pivot (5,8), i.e. the 2x2 at x4-5, y7-8.
# spitter_head [0] shut bud [1] open, watching [2] swollen, about to spit [3] spitting   (mouth at x14, y7-8)
# nettle_head  [0] coiled [1] reared back, red tip cocked, hairs up [2] the lash (hook at x35-37) [3] coming back
# rambler walks on its roots: _walk trot like the dog ([0] top-front + bottom-back root forward, [2] the others),
# _bite [0] bristling [1] three thorny vines lashing to x30, _rest rooted = an ordinary bush, _dead torn up.
# Colours: leaves G g v V (pale l veins, olive T sickly tips), nettle tendrils g G, hairs/thorns E,
# roots/vines n N W, spitter bloom y Y O with throat x R 0, acid l g X, roses Q P m, wilt T W N H.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- SPITTER (flowerbed plant that spits acid)
@frames spitter_base 2 16 16
